From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:12:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 129/144] GreatDANE: use Dane, not Pepecoin, as the Windows
 publisher; stub certs are TODO (round 4g)

Coordinator ruling: the Pepecoin company/publisher strings introduced in
round 4f are replaced.

Both module.ver files (browser/app and pbproxy):
- Company is Dane
- Copyright is Dane contributors, with a factual Mozilla.org credit and the
  MPL 2 notice
- Trademarks still credit Firefox and Mozilla to Mozilla.org

branding.nsi CompanyName is Dane (it was Pepecoin even before 4f; Windows
metadata should match). CertNameDownload and CertIssuerDownload are the
placeholder TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET, with a comment that no
Windows signing identity exists yet and that the publisher name is the
owner's decision before release. The defines stay syntactically valid NSIS.
The stub's PE trust check is still expected to fail until a real identity
is set.

pepecoin.surf update URLs and other existing site/bundle-id references are
unchanged; those are not publisher metadata.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
---
 browser/app/module.ver                  |  4 ++--
 browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver          |  4 ++--
 browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi | 17 +++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/app/module.ver b/browser/app/module.ver
index 4785bb26be..02871d0968 100644
--- a/browser/app/module.ver
+++ b/browser/app/module.ver
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
-WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Pepecoin
-WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=© Pepecoin. Includes Mozilla.org contributions; available under the MPL 2 license.
+WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Dane
+WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=© Dane contributors. Includes Mozilla.org contributions; available under the MPL 2 license.
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION=@MOZ_APP_WINVERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION_STRING=@MOZ_APP_VERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_TRADEMARKS=Firefox and Mozilla are trademarks of Mozilla.org in the U.S. and other countries.
diff --git a/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver b/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
index 4785bb26be..02871d0968 100644
--- a/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
+++ b/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
-WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Pepecoin
-WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=© Pepecoin. Includes Mozilla.org contributions; available under the MPL 2 license.
+WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Dane
+WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=© Dane contributors. Includes Mozilla.org contributions; available under the MPL 2 license.
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION=@MOZ_APP_WINVERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION_STRING=@MOZ_APP_VERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_TRADEMARKS=Firefox and Mozilla are trademarks of Mozilla.org in the U.S. and other countries.
diff --git a/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi b/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
index c3da93563b..0cd1267c31 100644
--- a/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
+++ b/browser/branding/greatdane/branding.nsi
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 # instead of BrandFullName and typically should not be modified.
 !define BrandFullNameInternal "Dane"
 !define BrandFullName         "Dane"
-!define CompanyName           "Pepecoin"
+!define CompanyName           "Dane"
 !define URLInfoAbout          "https://dane.surf/"
 !define HelpLink              "https://dane.surf/support/"
 
@@ -25,13 +25,14 @@
 !define URLSystemRequirements "https://dane.surf/support/"
 !define Channel "unofficial"
 
-# Do not keep Mozilla Corporation / Mozilla's DigiCert CA: Dane is not signed
-# as Mozilla, and the live Windows installer is not code-signed yet. These
-# values must be updated to the real subject CN and issuer when signing starts.
-# Until then the stub's PE trust check is expected to fail and fall back to
-# URLManualDownload (the Dane download page).
-!define CertNameDownload   "Pepecoin"
-!define CertIssuerDownload "Pepecoin"
+# TODO(windows-signing): no Windows signing identity exists yet. The publisher
+# name used here (CertNameDownload subject CN and CertIssuerDownload issuer)
+# is the owner's decision before release. These placeholders are syntactically
+# valid NSIS string defines and must be replaced with the real identity before
+# any signed stub is shipped. Until then the stub's PE trust check is expected
+# to fail and fall back to URLManualDownload (the Dane download page).
+!define CertNameDownload   "TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET"
+!define CertIssuerDownload "TODO-NO-WINDOWS-SIGNING-IDENTITY-YET"
 
 # Dialog units are used so the UI displays correctly with the system's DPI
 # settings.
